  "note": "Triennial election of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation, polled Wednesday 17 May 1967 on the three wards of 1936 (North, South, Waterside); 32 candidates for 15 councillors' seats (Derry Journal, 5 May 1967, p. 1). Result declared at 12.30 a.m. on 18 May. The Derry Journal prints Robert Stewart's vote as 2,877; the News-Letter's 2,832 is used because it agrees with the Journal's printed Unionist total of 17,198. The Journal gives a poll of just over 70 per cent; the News-Letter calls 4,648 the valid poll."
